Package: obfmesh-server
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Section: net
Priority: optional
Maintainer: obfmesh
Depends: python3 (>= 3.11), python3-venv, iproute2, iptables, wireguard-tools, logrotate, systemd
# Suggests, not Recommends: a reverse proxy is mandatory for the router to reach this
# server, but which one is the admin's decision - apt must not install a web server on
# its own and rewrite the HTTP setup of the box.
Suggests: caddy | nginx
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Description: obfmesh control plane (FastAPI/uvicorn)
 obfmesh runs N parallel "obfuscator + WireGuard" spokes between a router and this
 server so that the throughput ceiling of a single wg-obfuscator process (~135 Mbit/s,
 measured) stops being the limit.
 .
 This package installs the control plane: the REST API and the web panel on
 127.0.0.1:8080, the orchestrator that keeps swg{i}, the obfuscator processes and the
 NAT rules in the state stored in SQLite, and the obfmesh-ctl helper for local control
 without HTTP.
 .
 Two things are deliberately not here. The wg-obfuscator binary is not shipped: its
 path is a setting (PATCH /api/settings, obfuscator_bin). The reverse proxy is not
 configured: the service listens on loopback only, so publishing it on 443 with TLS is
 a separate, mandatory step - see /etc/obfmesh/caddy-snippet.txt after installation.
 .
 The Python dependencies are installed by the postinst into a virtualenv under
 /opt/obfmesh/.venv, from the network or from the wheels vendored into the package.
